   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3747"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa byams pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person3916"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bla ma dam pa bsod nams rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བླ་མ་དམ་པ་བསོད་ནམས་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><birth notBefore="1312-01-01" notAfter="1312-12-31">1312</birth><death notBefore="1375-01-01" notAfter="1375-12-31">1375</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1226</idno><idno type="APIS">3916</idno></person><person xml:id="person4094"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnas drug pa blo gros mtshungs med</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གནས་དྲུག་པ་བློ་གྲོས་མཚུངས་མེད</persName><birth notBefore="1300-01-01" notAfter="1330-12-31">after 1300 before 1330</birth><death notBefore="1371-01-01" notAfter="1400-12-31">after 1371 before 1400</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4094</idno><note type="comment">Sa skya pa scholar of the 14th c. Floruit 1330-1371 ([BAQ9MH4T]: 320 and 322-323).&#13;
Credited with a commentary on the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564) ([MKQ6FJV7]: 61, n. 7).</note></person><person xml:id="person5942"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">btsun pa ston gzhon</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བཙུན་པ་སྟོན་གཞོན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ston pa gzhon nu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs ston gzhon</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1287-12-31">after 1200 before 1287</birth><death notBefore="1297-01-01" notAfter="1330-12-31">after 1297 before 1330</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5942</idno><note type="comment">Van der Kuijp ([FEHIEFEB]: 143) lists as potential candidates: sKag pa ston gzhon (whom he discards as this contemporary of Sa skya Paṇḍita would have been too old), sBas pa ston gzhon (ID: 6651) (a possible option, although he is not explicitly associated with epistemology), and Cog ro ston gzhon (as the most likely option).&#13;
Understood by Sun Weijin to be the "'jam dbyangs ston gzhon" in the Pramāṇavārttika lineage mentioned by 'Gos Lo tsā ba ([FEHIEFEB]: 143).&#13;
He traveled to the Mongol court in China in the early 1280s and translated in Tibetan Xuanzang's (ca. 602-64) Chinese version of Śaṅkarasvāmin's Nyāyapraveśa ([FEHIEFEB]: 165).&#13;
A "ston gzhon" - maybe the same person - is also listed as the author of two works in the [8H6M69W4]:&#13;
- Lam 'bras gyi bshad pa gsung ngag nyi ma'i 'od zer in 230 folios&#13;
- Kun gyi sna lam du ma grags pa'i rin po che'i gsung 'ga' &lt;gnyan ston tshul rgyal dang ston gzhon gnyis kyis&gt; zin bris su mdzad pa rnams in 38 folios. ([FEHIEFEB]: 166).</note></person><person xml:id="person6153"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">g.yag ston sangs rgyas dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཡག་སྟོན་སངས་རྒྱས་དཔལ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">g.yag phrug sangs rgyas dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mi pham g.yag</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">g.yag mi pham chos rje</persName><birth notBefore="1350-01-01" notAfter="1350-12-31">1350</birth><death notBefore="1414-01-01" notAfter="1414-12-31">1414</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P7997</idno><idno type="APIS">6153</idno><note type="comment">A khu ching Shes rab rgya mtsho's Tho yig lists several work on the Perfection of wisdom for this scholar ([5RXEUKD9]: 529, No. 11518: phar phyin rin chen bang mdzod dgos 'dod stsol pa; No. 11519 phar phyin dka' 'grel; No. 11520: phar phyin bsdus don).</note></person><person xml:id="person6352"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lha ston zhig po bsod nams rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ལྷ་སྟོན་ཞིག་པོ་བསོད་ནམས་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lha sa ba ru mtshams pa shes rab rgyal mtshan</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1400-12-31">before 1400</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">6352</idno><note type="comment">Fl. early 14th c.</note></person><person xml:id="person6624"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang btsun mdo sde dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཞང་བཙུན་མདོ་སྡེ་དཔལ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">btsun pa mdo sde dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang mdo sde dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mdo sde dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang mdo sde pa</persName><birth notBefore="1220-01-01" notAfter="1220-12-31">1220</birth><death notBefore="1290-01-01" notAfter="1290-12-31">1290</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P7084</idno><idno type="APIS">6624</idno><note type="comment">"Author of a series of notes (zin bris) on the narrative tales that illustrate some of the points Sa skya Paṇḍita had made in his Thub pa'i dgongs pa rab gsal, tales he had heard from the master himself." ([FEHIEFEB]: 126)</note></person><person xml:id="person6741"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nya dbon kun dga' dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཉ་དབོན་ཀུན་དགའ་དཔལ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyag dbon kun dga' dpal ba</persName><birth notBefore="1285-01-01" notAfter="1285-12-31">1285</birth><death notBefore="1379-01-01" notAfter="1379-12-31">1379</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2010</idno><idno type="APIS">6741</idno></person><person xml:id="person7384"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ri khrod pa blo gros mtshungs med</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རི་ཁྲོད་པ་བློ་གྲོས་མཚུངས་མེད</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo gros brtan pa</persName><birth notBefore="1316-01-01" notAfter="1316-12-31">1316</birth><death notBefore="1358-01-01" notAfter="1358-12-31">1358</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3093</idno><idno type="APIS">7384</idno><note type="comment">Sa skya scholar and meditator. See [BAQ9MH4T]: 323-324.</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3746"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mahāyānasūtrālaṃkāra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mahāyānasūtrālaṃkārakārikā</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po mdo sde'i rgyan zhes bya ba'i tshig le'ur byas pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mdo sde rgyan</title><author ref="person:3747">maitreya</author><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3746</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4635"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po'i mdo sde'i rgyan gyi dka' ba'i gnas bshad pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཐེག་པ་ཆེན་པོའི་མདོ་སྡེའི་རྒྱན་གྱི་དཀའ་བའི་གནས་བཤད་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shAkya'i dge slong bsod nams rgyal mtshan gyis mdzad pa'i theg pa chen po mdo sde rgyan gyi dka' gnad bshad pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po'i mdo sde rgyan gyi dka' gnad bshad pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po'i mdo' sde'i rgyan gyi dka' ba'i gnas bshad pa</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1322-01-01" notAfter="1375-12-31">after 1322 before 1375</date><author ref="person:3916">bla ma dam pa bsod nams rgyal mtshan</author><author ref="person:6352">lha ston zhig po bsod nams rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">[JZP4CZRX] connects this work with Bla ma dam pa bSod nams rgyal mtshan (ID:3916) (1327-1344), [S635TW6P]:91 with lHa ston zhig po bSod nams rgyal mtshan (ID:6352), the 13th abbot of gSang phu gling sTod.</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3746"/><idno type="APIS">4635</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5225"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dbus mtha'i 'grel pa dbu ma'i snang ba zhes bya ba'i bsdus don</title><title xml:lang="bo">དབུས་མཐའི་འགྲེལ་པ་དབུ་མའི་སྣང་བ་ཞེས་བྱ་བའི་བསྡུས་དོན</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dbus mtha'i bsdus don</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1322-01-01" notAfter="1375-12-31">after 1322 before 137